\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The aging asymmetry on the original cohort and on the external validation dataset. Aging is $\mathrm  {AUC}$ lost from early to late test with training held fixed; asymmetry is personal $-$ pooled aging, positive when the subject's own decoder ages more. Both rows use the same session-held-out protocol and the same count-matched control. $p$: paired sign-flip permutation.}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:allen}{{2}{7}{The aging asymmetry on the original cohort and on the external validation dataset. Aging is $\auc $ lost from early to late test with training held fixed; asymmetry is personal $-$ pooled aging, positive when the subject's own decoder ages more. Both rows use the same session-held-out protocol and the same count-matched control. $p$: paired sign-flip permutation}{table.2}{}}
